  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\int \\mathrm{e}^x\\left(\\frac{x \\sin ^{-1} x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}+\\frac{\\sin ^{-1} x}{\\left(1-x^2\\right)^{3 / 2}}+\\frac{x}{1-x^2}\\right) \\mathrm{d} x=\\mathrm{g}(x)+\\mathrm{C}$, where C is the constant of integration, then $g\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$ equals :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ilQIC",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\sqrt{\\frac{e}{3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5J554",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\sqrt{\\frac{e}{3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wnOfK",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\sqrt{\\frac{e}{2}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHtNj",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\sqrt{\\frac{e}{2}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d}{d x}\\left(\\frac{x \\cdot \\sin ^{-1} x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\right)-\\sin ^{-1} x \\cdot\\left(\\frac{1 \\cdot \\sqrt{1-x^2}+\\frac{x \\cdot 2 x}{2 \\sqrt{1-x^2}}}{1-x^2}\\right) \\\\\n& =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}} \\\\\n& =\\frac{\\sin ^{-1} x}{\\left(1-x^2\\right)^{3 / 2}}+\\frac{x}{1-x^2}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Hence, } I=\\int e^x\\left(f(x)+f^{\\prime}(x)\\right) d x \\\\\n& =e^x \\cdot f(x)+C \\\\\n& I=e^x \\cdot \\frac{x \\cdot \\sin ^{-1} x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}+C=g(x)+C \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow g(x)=\\frac{x e^x \\sin ^{-1} x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}} \\text { and } g(1 / 2)=\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\sqrt{\\frac{e}{3}}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
